# /usr/sbin/skydsecd is linked statically on purpose.
#
# The daemon reports on the integrity of the host it runs on.  If it resolved
# its dependencies through shared objects on that host, a compromised host
# could substitute one and control what the daemon reports about it -- which
# would defeat the point of running the check at all.
#
# This is why the program also avoids getpwuid()/getgrgid(): NSS dlopen()s
# its modules at runtime even from a statically linked binary, so those calls
# would have reintroduced exactly the dependency the static link removes.
# The uid/gid comparison is done against the raw st_uid/st_gid instead.
#
# Overridden rather than left to fire so that a genuinely unexpected static
# binary appearing in this package is not lost in known output.
skydsecd: statically-linked-binary [usr/sbin/skydsecd]
skydsecd: statically-linked-binary [usr/sbin/skydsecd-rust]

